{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"727","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Guess the Array"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is an interactive problem. You should use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation after each printed line. For example, in C++ you should use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", in Java you should use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and in Pascal — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you should guess an array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" which is unknown for you. The only information you have initially is the length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only allowed action is to ask the sum of two elements by their indices. Formally, you can print two indices "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the indices should be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then your program should read the response: the single integer equals to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai + aj"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is easy to prove that it is always possible to guess the array using at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" requests."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Write a program that will guess the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" by making at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" requests."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In each test your program should guess a single array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input starts with a line containing integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 5000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of the array. Your program should read it at first."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After that your program should print to the standard output the requests about the sum of two elements or inform that the array is guessed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In case your program is making a request to ask the sum of two elements, it should print line in the format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"? i j"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" are distinct integers between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"j"},{"kind":"text","text":" are indices in the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In case your program informs that the array is guessed, it should print line in the format \""},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"! a1 a2 ... an"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (it is guaranteed that all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" are positive integers not exceeding "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"105"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th element of the array "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The response on a request is a single integer equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai + aj"},{"kind":"text","text":", printed on a separate line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your program can do at most "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" requests. Note that the final line «"},{"children":[{"kind":"math_inline","text":"! a1 a2 ... an"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"» is not counted as a request."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Do not forget about "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operation after each printed line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After you program prints the guessed array, it should terminate normally."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n \n9\n \n7\n \n9\n \n11\n \n6\n "}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":" \n? 1 5\n \n? 2 3\n \n? 4 1\n \n? 5 2\n \n? 3 4\n \n! 4 6 1 5 5"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The format of a test to make a hack is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The first line contains an integer number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 5000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the length of the array."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the elements of the array to guess. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"727C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/727/problem/C"}